      "claim": "The minimum diameter of an adult human skull is significantly larger than the maximum diameter of the human birth canal.",
      "evidence": "An adult human skull has a minimum cross-sectional diameter (often near the foramen magnum or narrowest point) of approximately 11-12 cm, whereas the widest part of the maternal pelvic inlet is typically 10-11 cm, and the outlet is smaller. Even the smallest adult skulls exceed the dimensions of the birth canal.",
      "weight": 0.4,
