      "reason_rejected": "This would require the skull to be smaller than the pelvic inlet or deformable, neither of which is true for a standard adult human skull. While extremely small individuals might have smaller pelvises, the skull size scales similarly, and the rigid nature of the adult skull remains the primary barrier. Even in pathological cases of pelvic fracture, the skull would be destroyed, failing the condition of 'passing through' as an intact object."
